.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-config - Manage persisted CLI defaults (e.g. base-url)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 config [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage persisted CLI defaults stored in the config file.

.PP
Run bare to list every setting with its effective value and where it comes from.
Resolution precedence is: flag  >  env var  >  config file  >  built-in default.

.PP
Only non-sensitive values are stored — never private keys or tokens.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for config


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 config
  rail0 config set base-url http://localhost:9292
  rail0 config get base-url
  rail0 config unset base-url
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-get(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-path(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-set(1)\fP, \fBrail0-config-unset(1)\fP
